4 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=3.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{7}+16\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\frac{10}{7} \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08e8ef20-2a38-5e05-81da-697f538105e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436003 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436004 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a774054b-3577-5411-a266-873c0fe2ca4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436004 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436005 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436005 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b23b860b-4012-51e9-9c6f-d158c0177636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436005 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436006 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436006 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d680df42-9af5-5d8e-85c5-ee68af73edc3" #